1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
There are racing drivers without a paid race engineer.
APEX is for them.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:25,000
A professional race engineer costs four to five hundred pounds a day.
Every Formula One driver has one. Most adaptive racers, veteran-team
drivers, and grassroots competitors do not. After the FIA revision
in late 2017 lifted the single-seater ban on disabled drivers,
the barrier stopped being regulatory. It became economic.

3
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Britcar Trophy 2026. Lap 17 of 19 at Donington Park.
Sarah Reynolds is two tenths off her PB. Time bleeding out
in Sector 2 at Old Hairpin. Her debrief: lost the rears mid
Old Hairpin again, can't trail-brake on the lever the way
she did at Croft last month.

4
00:00:42,000 --> 00:01:30,000
APEX runs on the same IBM Granite stack that ships to
Scuderia Ferrari, pointed at the drivers who need a race
engineer most. Three layers. Granite TimeSeries TTM r2.1
channel-mix decoder fine-tune per D-010 Track 1. Differentiable
Cvxpylayers physics projection at constant mu. 8-tier Pacejka
linearization + SCP outer-loop + jerk-bound enforcement are
deferred swap-points named in D-031. Granite Guardian 4.1 8B
BYOC audits every projection log. Granite Instruct writes
the report. TTM forecasts the envelope. Instruct writes the
tuning delta. Aggregation done honestly.

5
00:01:30,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Three structural moats. First pretrained TSFM on adaptive
motorsport telemetry. First public AI race-engineer workflow
we found that reads the FIA Certificate of Adaptations as
binding regulatory input. First COA-parameterized brake-throttle
simultaneity gate. Sarah's hand-control hardware permits
simultaneity. Her COA permits it. The V1 NumPy validator reads
coa_overlap_flag and routes the constraint per-driver. We coach
disabled drivers with the model that matches their car.

6
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Sixty seconds after Sarah uploads her telemetry, APEX returns:
a corner-by-corner coaching report, a tuning recommendation
reduce hand-lever brake travel by four millimetres citing the
exact COA section, a next-session envelope forecast, and a
Granite Guardian safety stamp with the reasoning trace visible.
Every claim cites a specific COA section and a specific FIA
Appendix L provision. Provenance on every line.

7
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Fourteen IBM Granite tools on a per-tool honesty ladder.
Granite-Docling, Vision, TimeSeries TTM, FlowState, TSPulse,
Embedding R2, Guardian, Instruct 4.1 8B + 3B, Speech 4.1
2B-Plus, Nano WebGPU edge, LangGraph + MCP + ContextForge
orchestration, Docling library + Mellea as accelerators.
Stephen Sookra and Vinh Le. Kennesaw State University.
Twelve days. Public from Day 1. Apache 2.0.

8
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:58,000
APEX is a reference architecture for governed foundation-model
deployment on safety-critical sensor data. The race engineer
for the drivers who do not have one.

9
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
